☑ Phase 2 — Reevaluate water-test necessity and overlapping coverage
  Review and disposition record (2026-11-03)
    The necessity review used existing source/receipts without new executions. The user then
    approved both reductions A/B and retention of all other rows and motion samples.
    Scope is the three water families selected by this plan, compared with existing receiver,
    UV/pixel-normal, reduction, production-liquid, transport and publication/lifecycle witnesses.
    The inherited performance analyses require preserved independent references, failure
    attribution, numerical bounds and lifecycle coverage; elapsed cost alone cannot justify removal.
    Current contracts: [PBR.WaterRefraction.md](PBR.WaterRefraction.md), sections Background
    resolution and bilateral receivers, Optics and traversal, Water quality and receiver contract,
    and Validation and remaining acceptance; [PBR.Liquids.md](PBR.Liquids.md), Material and optics
    and Validation and acceptance. Historical receiver-baseline descriptions do not replace
    the current bounded-traversal and producer-validated-depth contract.
    Test source paths below are relative to ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/GPU/. Shader include
    paths such as liquids/receiver.glsl are relative to
    ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded/assets/vanillagraphicsexpanded/shaders/includes/.
  Inventory before the approved reductions, and contract mapping
    WaterRefractionDiagnosticTests.BaselineReceiverDiagnostics: 72 rows = scenarios 0..11
    × budgets {2,4,8} × half {false,true}. Sample (64,64), except edge-motion samples
    x={1,3,6,12,32,64}, y=64: 102 observed pixels per full selection. Seven MRT outputs are
    produced; assertions/readbacks use decision, last sample, transport and work (0/1/2/6).
    Sampled UV/depth and transport length/direction/fallback/receiver Z are finite/logged,
    not independently predicted numerical values, except the positive-Z sign check below.
    Selection, receiver-position and receiver-radiance MRT outputs 3/4/5 are not read here.
    Every row checks finite decision/sample/transport, evaluations within budget, confidence one
    for accepted hits, zero spatial radiance blends, selected-triangle/color-fetch accounting
    and depth-fetch bounds. Viewport/scissor restoration and clean GL error state are asserted.
      0 flat, 1 tilted, 2 one-centimetre separation: accepted geometric support.
      3 adjacent foreground: accepted support with success reason, rather than blanket rejection.
      4 sky: unavailable-data reason; no selected color reads.
      5 range exhaustion: reason 9, exactly two evaluations, no selected radiance/triangle blend.
      6 edge motion: all six columns accepted without confidence fade.
      7 long path: accepted without distance-confidence fade; path length itself is not asserted.
      8 positive view-Z: refracted Z positive; accepted at budget 8, lower-budget validity unasserted.
      9 metadata: unavailable-data reason, currently the same depth-sentinel path as scenario 4.
      10 depth discontinuity, 11 grazing: no geometric hit.
    These rows exercise shared raw traversal through the diagnostic shader, not the compiled
    production quality/resolution selectors or final OIT composition. They complement those tests.
    WaterShallowContinuityTests.ShallowWallMotionPreservesContinuousRadiance: 24 rows =
    quality {0,1,2,3} × half {false,true} × {planar 20 cm, shoreline 3 cm, curved 12 cm}.
    Each retains all 201 ordered motions (4,824 total), valid/full-confidence selection,
    explicit RAY/UV provenance, affine X-to-HDR-red association within .0001, and adjacent
    HDR-red jumps at most .01. Planar rows also check their independently authored plane.
    Quality 0 additionally checks submerged support and bounded lookup work, plus 201 direct
    filter samples per row with the same .01 continuity bound (1,206 direct-filter samples).
    Motion range is ±.006 for shoreline and ±.04 otherwise. The curved rows do not duplicate
    the planar reference. Method/switch counts are logged, not required transition counts;
    the budget transition test supplies that separate witness. Retain every row and motion.
    WaterRefractionBudgetTests: 32 rows across six methods:
      ClippedEndpointPreservesFallback (8): qualities 1/2/3 × full/half, plus quality 3 tiny
      extents × full/half. Invalid and valid source scenes check seed/endpoint evaluation,
      projected endpoint, selected/standalone-UV equivalence and a second-probe accepted hit.
      Tiny extents independently prove positive movement within the same texture footprint.
      RayAndUvTransitionsStayWithinReceiverFootprint (4): slopes {1,4} × full/half, 61 motions
      each. Independent Snell/plane intersection and affine RGB checks bound transition error
      by receiver footprint. Full rows require 61 ray hits; half rows require actual switches.
      CachedPatchRequiresRepresentedCoverage (2): ordinary and irregular-source hulls. Ordinary
      support checks one evaluation, ray provenance and corrected-hit color. Irregular support
      currently checks only two evaluations; it does not assert final rejection/provenance.
      ExhaustionAndTirAccountForEveryLookup (6): qualities 1/2/3 × TIR false/true. No hit or
      selected method; exhaustion checks min(2^quality,6) ray evaluations and zero UV lookups;
      TIR checks zero ray/UV evaluations. Only the repeated TIR rows are consolidation candidates.
      ExhaustedFallbackReusesInitialSupport (6): qualities 1/2/3 × full/half, each across
      {exhausted,invalid-seed,invalid-later,edge,offscreen}. Raw ray, dispatcher and standalone
      UV outputs check original-seed reuse, validity/transport/position/radiance equivalence,
      saved seed depth reads, UV lookup accounting and zero work for offscreen rejection.
      TierSelectionTracksDenseReference (6): qualities 1/2/3 × full/half, four scenes
      {floor,thin,gap,discontinuity} × seven motions. All scenes retain work ceilings and
      valid-hit confidence/radiance checks; geometric hits must lie on an authored depth layer.
      Floor rows independently bound position and adjacent motion error, including the reduced
      UV approximation footprint, and require seven accepted selections. Dense-reference
      misses/errors for other scenes are reported, not bounded correctness assertions.
  Overlap and retained witnesses
    WaterRefractionTests.OpaqueHitsAndUnavailableSourcesHaveDefinedComposition (95 rows) uses
    the actual compiled liquid variants and independent composition/coordinate references,
    including TIR across qualities/resolutions. It does not expose raw traversal work counters.
    WaterReceiverFilterTests (20 rows after the related-suite reduction below) isolates
    support eligibility, incompatible layers,
    malformed RGBA, source provenance, grazing planes and false coplanar depth columns.
    WaterRefractionReductionTests (6 correctness rows) checks paired selection, alpha/depth
    validity, tie order, half-float limits and odd edges, not moving traversal/fallback behavior.
    WaterUvRefractionTests (37 rows) independently checks Snell projection, thin paths, edge
    continuity, seed repair, TIR and camera-to-interface length for standalone UV fallback.
    WaterPixelNormalRefractionTests (12 rows) checks the distinct quality-0 normal-detail rule,
    saturation, shallow scaling, invalid candidates and TIR. Neither suite replaces the 201-point
    integrated shallow sweeps or the mandatory ray/UV transition witness.
    WaterTransportTests checks linear composition and photon directions. Resolution, lifecycle,
    capture-state and overlay-composition tests own publication/state/resize/disposal guarantees;
    synthetic diagnostic MRT tests do not replace those integration boundaries. Retain them.
  Initial approved dispositions
    A — Consolidate diagnostic scenario 9 into scenario 4: remove six metadata rows, retain
    all six sky rows and all other diagnostic rows. Fixtures/WaterReceiverTestInputs.cs encodes
    every alpha-zero sample to depth 1; liquids/receiver.glsl rejects depth 1 before color reads.
    At full size both scenes therefore take the same unavailable-depth path; half reduction
    also rejects their depth before color. Surface/normal and all asserted sampler guarantees
    are otherwise identical. Lost coverage is the duplicate authored metadata label, not an
    independent metadata-validation path. FilterKeepsOnlyCompatibleReceiverSupport's full/half
    mixed-invalid rows retain helper alpha conversion and zero-color-read assertions;
    its full/nonfinite row retains partial unavailable support, and its inconsistent rows retain
    malformed-pair rejection. Reduction's candidate-validity checks
    and actual liquid scenario 3 retain independent invalid-metadata producer/consumer checks.
    B — Remove only ExhaustionAndTirAccountForEveryLookup rows (quality=1,tir=true) and
    (quality=2,tir=true); retain (3,true) and all three non-TIR rows. The dynamic selector maps
    these positive qualities to a budget, then the shared ray helper returns for TIR before
    using that budget or fetching depth/color. The surviving row asserts the same NONE result
    and zero ray/UV evaluations. Production TIR variants remain covered separately. Lost
    coverage is repeating that budget-independent early exit with two other dynamic constants.
    C — Keep all other rows and every motion sample. No whole test family is proven unnecessary.
    Do not delete the irregular-hull row or non-floor dense-reference scenes solely because
    their assertions are incomplete; retain them as unresolved coverage-quality follow-ups.
    Any future strengthening must state the missing oracle explicitly rather than claiming
    the current test already proves it. Exact work assertions protect documented bounds/reuse;
    they are not dismissed wholesale as private implementation details.
    The initial A/B approval retained 120 cases (66 diagnostic, 24 continuity,
    30 budget). No assertions, tolerances, samples, fixtures or production code otherwise change.
    Implementation scope is removal of only those eight rows and test-local branches used only
    by removed scenario 9. Surviving scenario IDs, assertions, tolerances, textures, shaders and
    fixtures remain unchanged. Verification must establish exact retained membership, passing
    retained diagnostics and zero-work TIR assertions, and passing independent metadata and
    compiled-production TIR witnesses in Debug/Release. Unchanged continuity and other budget
    methods retain their existing source/receipt evidence. Phase 4's 201/61-motion contract
    remains unchanged. Setup reuse/batching can preserve that coverage without deletion.
    Separate setup opportunity: before the further matrix reduction below, the continuity test
    constructed its direct-filter program and three-attachment target in all 24 rows but used
    them only in six quality-0 rows. The approved seven-row selection still constructs them
    in every row but uses them in only three, leaving four rows with unused filter setup.
    Avoiding that setup would preserve all observations. This remains a future optimization,
    outside the parameter-removal scope and without a measured savings claim.
