    finite validation and full-domain extrema. No floating arithmetic flushes subnormal peaks.
    Independent authored GPU cases cover alpha exclusion, signed RGB, a 67-pixel tail with
    the maximum in the final group, fresh same-storage writes, result reset, signed zero,
    subnormals, finite limits, RGB/alpha NaN and infinities, and retired observation ownership.
    Temporary runtime measurement passed 1/1. On the same published final image, the executed
    legacy pair used two result images, dispatches and readbacks, returning 256 result bytes;
