☑ Phase 12 — Consolidate overlapping checks and reduce repeated integration combinations
  Scope and evidence (2026-11-06)
    Cover all 20 proposed case reductions from the read-only audit: 14 prioritized reductions
    plus six lower-priority candidates. Counts describe net discovered-case reductions, not
    eliminated assertions or guaranteed runtime savings. Paths below are relative to
    ../VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests/. Preserve the accepted work and historical counts of
    Phases 1–11, and inherit the shared requirements and Rendering.RepresentativeTestCoverage.todo.
    The latest qualified retained-cache Release run is 411.182s, with 5,952 passed, six reconciled
    skips and zero failures across 5,958 runtime names. Evidence is under
    ../TestResults/TestRuntimeOptimizations/Phase11/final-full-release/.
    The five proposed surface-lighting matrix removals account for 8.90s of individual case
    durations; the two atmosphere quality endpoints account for 3.14s. The three water rows
    account for 1.37s, while the entire eight-row overlay suite accounts for only .61s.
    These historical case times prioritize investigation; they are not additive wall savings.
    The remaining 111.182s gap to five minutes is not demonstrated recoverable by these changes.
    This phase plans test changes only. Do not change production rendering, stress workloads,
    runner selection, GPU parallelism, process boundaries or the accepted executable-owner
    deferrals. Do not reopen AO direct/composite sharing or direct-probe/water class ownership.
  Execution evidence (2026-11-06; independently audited and accepted)
